---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';

const title = 'About | JVV Digital';
const description = 'Meet Will Johntz Van Voris, founder of JVV Digital. A practical, technical approach to AI visibility, SEO, and website builds.';

const founderSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Will Johntz Van Voris',
  jobTitle: 'Founder',
  worksFor: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'JVV Digital'
  },
  alumniOf: {
    '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity',
    name: 'Siena University'
  }
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/about" structuredData={founderSchema}>
  <section class="site-container pt-12 md:pt-16">
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="surface-strong p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-jvv-dark md:text-5xl">Built by someone who likes solving the technical side of modern discovery</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Hi, I am Will Johntz Van Voris, founder of JVV Digital. I started the business because I was fascinated by the new world of marketing for AI and wanted my work to help people in a real and practical way.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="surface p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-jvv-orange">A little context</div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          I was first introduced to computer science in my freshman year of college after my original major, physics, was not going especially well. Once I got into computer science, I was quickly hooked. I liked the logic, the structure, and the feeling of building something useful from clear technical choices.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Near the end of college I learned more about digital marketing and then, more specifically, marketing for AI. That was the moment the work started to feel like the right fit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-container py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-center">
      <div class="surface p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="eyebrow">Why JVV Digital exists</div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          When I first found out about answer engine optimization, I was surprised by how little the subject was being talked about. Even in technical conversations, the terminology was still new enough that people were not really using it yet.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          I asked my software engineering professor, who was also my advisor, about AEO at the time, and she had not even heard the term. That made the opportunity feel very clear to me. I wanted to be early, stay curious, and build something useful before the space got crowded.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="surface-strong p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="eyebrow">How I think about the work</div>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-jvv-dark">Intent first, no shortcuts, no patchwork</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          I believe that effective marketing starts with intent. I look at who the business wants to reach, what it needs to market, and how it wants to come across, then I build a plan that checks those boxes without sacrificing quality, reputation, or authority.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          If the plan needs to change, I change it. If the business needs a clearer starting point, I help define that first. The point is to do the work carefully enough that it still makes sense later.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-container py-16 md:py-20">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Working style"
      title="Collaborative, consultative, and easy to follow"
      copy="You tell me the goal, I tell you how to get there, and we keep refining the plan until the direction feels right."
      center
    />

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="surface-strong p-6">
        <div class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-jvv-orange">01</div>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-jvv-dark">Share the goal</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">You tell me what you are trying to achieve and who you are trying to reach.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-strong p-6">
        <div class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-jvv-orange">02</div>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-jvv-dark">Shape the plan</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">I suggest the technical and strategic path, then we adjust it together if something better fits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-strong p-6">
        <div class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-jvv-orange">03</div>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-jvv-dark">Act and reflect</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">The work gets implemented, results are tracked, and the approach evolves based on what actually happens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-container py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.9fr] lg:items-center">
      <div class="surface-dark p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="eyebrow border-white/10 bg-white/10 text-white/90">Why this stays relevant</div>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">AI and search keep evolving, so the process has to keep evolving too</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-white/80">
          I stay focused on research, trial and error, and measured adjustments so the work does not fall behind the market. The goal is to keep learning while staying practical.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-strong p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-jvv-orange">What I value</div>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-jvv-blue"></span><span>Curiosity that leads to better decisions</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-jvv-orange"></span><span>Practical work that produces useful outcomes</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-jvv-blue"></span><span>Collaboration that keeps the plan grounded</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="mt-1 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-jvv-orange"></span><span>Reflection that keeps the process honest</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-container py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="surface p-8 md:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:items-center">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Let us begin this partnership</div>
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-jvv-dark md:text-4xl">If you are thinking seriously about visibility, I would be glad to help shape the path</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Whether you need to improve an existing site, rebuild the foundation, or plan something from scratch, the first step is a clear conversation about what the business actually needs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Start your free review</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
